# Local development settings. Copy to `.env` — git-ignored — and edit.
#
# These are the names the chart sets, so what you put here is what an operator would
# configure. The dev server inlines them the way the container renders them at startup,
# so a change needs no restart but does need a full page reload.
#
# Only the keys below reach the browser: `CORE_ENV_KEYS` in `src/env.ts` for the
# application's own, and anything named `EXTENSION_*` for an installed extension's.


# --- Settings the application reads ---

# Serve the whole API from in-browser fixtures. Off unless asked for, in a dev server
# exactly as in a built image — a backend that is down should not render as a healthy
# app full of plausible data. On, it overrides every backend setting below, and anything
# reporting who is signed in says nobody is.
#
# `?mock=ok|empty|error|slow` picks which scenario the fixtures play, and does nothing
# unless this is already on.
# ENABLE_MOCK_UI=true

# Where the browser calls the API. Relative by default, which the dev server proxies.
# API_BASE_URL=/api

# Where the dev server sends those calls. Read by `vite.config.ts`, so it never reaches
# the browser. Defaults to the controller on 8083, which is what
# `scripts/setup-cluster/setup-cluster.sh` forwards — a cluster from that script needs
# nothing here. Point it at 8080 to go through the UI pod's nginx instead, which is the
# hop a deployment takes.
# KAGENT_DEV_CONTROLLER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# Chat stream inactivity timeout, in milliseconds.
# STREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# Where "Sign in with SSO" sends the browser.
# SSO_REDIRECT_PATH=/oauth2/start


# --- Settings an installed extension reads ---
#
# Anything named `EXTENSION_*` is passed through untouched. The application reads none
# of them and does not know what they mean; the extension that reads them documents
# them. Nothing needs adding here for an extension to gain one.


# --- An installed extension's own settings go below this line ---
#
# Read by an extension's tooling rather than by the application, so it never reaches the
# browser. A branch that installs an extension appends here instead of editing above,
# which keeps merging this file a merge rather than a negotiation.
